\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Pretraining compute budget}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{compute}

\p{A \newvocab{pretraining compute budget} is an upper bound
#{C_{\rm pre}} on a declared cost measure for the complete pretraining run.
The declaration must say whether it counts arithmetic operations, accelerator
time, energy, or another resource.}

\p{Hoffmann et al. state their FLOP calculation in
\citet{app. F}{hoffmann2022training}. Kaplan et al. relate parameter count,
training tokens, and compute in
\citet{sec. 2.1}{kaplan2020scaling}. A FLOP estimate and elapsed time are
different measures. FTIP will not substitute one for the other without an
explicit conversion model.}
